              "pitfalls": "React compares the new state with `Object.is`. The same array reference is `===`-equal to the previous one, so React skips the re-render. The list looks unchanged. Replace with a copy:  The setter triggers another render, which triggers the setter again, which triggers another render. Move the logic into an event handler or an effect with the right dependency list.  // after every setItems call: setFirstItem(items[0] ?? null); ```  This duplicates the source of truth and creates a sync bug the moment the derivation races with an update. Derive during render instead:  State is for values that change independently of props and other state. Anything that can be computed from existing state or props should be a `const` in the same render."
