        "total_duration_seconds": 590,
        "summary_notes": {
          "definition": "Imagine a subscription desk. Each time you hand the clerk a brand-new key, even if it opens the same door, the clerk treats it as a different key: the old subscription is cancelled and a new one starts. A callback created during render is like that new key. `useCallback` can keep the same function object between renders. `useRef` gives you a small drawer whose address stays fixed while its contents can change.",
          "mental_model": "Subscriptions, timers, debounced work, and memoized list rows often use identity to decide whether to restart or re-render. Stable identity prevents needless teardown and child work. `useEffectEvent` avoids the opposite bug: adding every value to an Effect dependency list can reconnect a chat room whenever a theme changes. Refs also bridge React's declarative render model to DOM focus and third-party widgets. These tools do not make every render faster; they make a measured identity boundary predictable.",
          "code_example": "import { memo, useCallback, useRef, useState } from \"react\";\n\nconst SaveButton = memo(function SaveButton({ onSave }: { onSave: () => void }) {\n  console.log(\"SaveButton rendered\");\n  return <button onClick={onSave}>Save</button>;\n});\n\nexport function Editor() {\n  const [text, setText] = useState(\"\");\n  const onSave = useCallback(() => console.log(text), [text]);\n  const inputRef = useRef<HTMLInputElement>(null);\n  return <><input ref={inputRef} value={text} onChange={(e) => setText(e.target.value)} /><SaveButton onSave={onSave} /></>;\n}",
          "pitfalls": "- **Using `useMemo` for a function.** `useMemo(() => () => save(id), [id])` works, but `useCallback(() => save(id), [id])` states the intent directly. `useMemo` caches a result; `useCallback` caches a function. - **Leaving a reactive value out.** `useCallback(() => console.log(text), [])` captures the initial `text`. With the exhaustive-deps rule, you may see `React Hook useCallback has a missing dependency: 'text'.` Fix it with `[text]`, or use a ref when latest non-rendering data is deliberately required. - **Expecting a ref update to paint.** `ref.current = value` does not render new JSX. Use `useState` for visible data. - **Calling hooks conditionally.** `if (enabled) useCallback(...)` causes `Error: Rendered fewer hooks than expected.` Call hooks at the top level, then branch inside the callback or render."
        },
