        "id": "04-005",
        "number": 5,
        "title": "Zod to JSON Schema conversion",
        "local_chapter_file": "005-zod-to-json-schema-conversion.md",
        "key_concepts": [
          "1. Hook: two labels for the same package",
          "2. The concept",
          "3. Minimal example",
          "4. Predict the result",
          "5. Common mistakes",
          "6. Why this matters"
        ],
        "total_duration_seconds": 1096,
        "summary_notes": {
          "definition": "Imagine a package at a shipping counter. The warehouse uses an internal label with detailed handling instructions. A public carrier accepts a standard label format. You can keep the warehouse label for your own code, then print a JSON Schema label when another system needs to understand the package.  A Zod schema is the internal label. JSON Schema is a portable description of JSON data. `z.toJSONSchema()` prints the portable description. `z.fromJSONSchema()` reads one back into a Zod schema.",
          "mental_model": "You meet this boundary when a React form shares its contract with a route handler, an OpenAPI generator, an AI model, or another language. The Zod schema remains the runtime gate inside the app. The generated JSON Schema gives tools outside the app a common shape to inspect.  The split prevents a particular class of bugs: a UI can appear type-safe while its HTTP payload, generated API document, and runtime parser disagree. Keeping `z.input`, `z.output`, and the exported JSON Schema visible makes coercion, defaults, required keys, and unsupported JavaScript values explicit.",
          "code_example": "import { z } from \"zod\";\n\nconst Profile = z.object({\n  displayName: z.string().min(1),\n  age: z.int().min(0),\n});\n\ntype Profile = z.infer<typeof Profile>;\n\nexport function SchemaPreview() {\n  const jsonSchema = z.toJSONSchema(Profile);\n\n  return (\n    <section>\n      <h2>Profile contract</h2>\n      <pre>{JSON.stringify(jsonSchema, null, 2)}</pre>\n    </section>\n  );\n}",
          "pitfalls": "This deliberately broken call throws at runtime:  z.toJSONSchema(z.date()); ```  The runtime error is an `Error` about an unrepresentable type, commonly shown as:  Use an ISO string schema when the wire format is JSON:  Or use `{ unrepresentable: \"any\" }` only when the receiving system can safely handle an unconstrained value."
        },
