              "mental_model": "The `--color-*` namespace is the connective tissue between a Tailwind project and its brand. Every UI control that takes a colour (backgrounds, text, borders, rings, outlines, SVG fill and stroke, form-control accents, insertion cursors, text-decoration lines, shadow colour, scrollbar colour, dividers between children, gradient stops) reads from the same namespace. Designing a colour once, then letting that single declaration plumb through fourteen utility families, is the design-system guarantee the rest of the styling chapter builds on.  You will meet the surrounding utilities in every styled component from here on: text-decoration utilities paint brand underlines on links, the slash-opacity form appears in half the design-token rules, the `divide-*` family gives list views their visual rhythm, SVG utilities paint icon-colour-through-text-colour through the `fill-current` pair. The internalisation of \"the prefix names the property; the namespace names the family\" is what makes reading a Tailwind class list feel like reading CSS.",
              "code_example": "@theme {\n  --color-brand-500: oklch(0.62 0.16 256);\n}",
