              "mental_model": "A 2D transform lives on the page plane (X and Y). A 3D transform adds depth (Z). `translate-z-12` writes `transform: translate3d(0, 0, 12px)` (or the equivalent matrix call), pushing the element 12 pixels toward the viewer. Without a perspective on the ancestor, the value is a flat translate; the element moves \"toward the camera\" only visually. With `transform-3d` (which writes `transform-style: preserve-3d`) on an ancestor that has `perspective` set, the move reads as actual depth.  The Z translation only renders visibly when there is a `perspective` somewhere up the tree. The most common source of \"nothing happened\" is a missing `perspective-[value]` on a grandparent. Tailwind ships `perspective-near` (small depth), `perspective-far` (large depth), `perspective-<number>` (a numeric scale), and the arbitrary/pixel forms.",
