              "mental_model": "The `ThemeProvider` is a React context provider whose value is a fully built `Theme` object. `createTheme(options)` walks the options, fills every unset token from a default, and returns a complete, deeply-typed `Theme`. The provider hands that theme down the tree, and every MUI component (and every `styled` / `sx` / `useTheme` call) reads it from context. Move the provider, change the theme; the visible app re-themes without a single prop-drilled colour.  When two styling systems coexist in the same tree (MUI plus Theme UI, MUI plus Chakra, MUI plus a custom design-token context), the providers must agree on which context key carries which theme. MUI exposes `THEME_ID` for exactly that negotiation: a string constant you put on a non-default context, so MUI's `styled`, `sx`, and `useTheme` look up the right value while other libraries keep using the default key.",
