        "id": "05-050",
        "number": 50,
        "title": "Material UI Grid v2 migration (and a roundup: `theme.typography` and the `Typography`/`Link` components, `theme.transitions`, reduced motion, `ImageList`, `Tooltip`, the `ClassNameGenerator` build-time hook)",
        "local_chapter_file": "050-material-ui-grid-v2-migration.md",
        "key_concepts": [
          "Mental model",
          "Grid v2 migration",
          "`theme.typography` and the `Typography` component",
          "`Link`",
          "`theme.transitions` and reduced motion",
          "`ImageList`"
        ],
        "total_duration_seconds": 798,
        "summary_notes": {
          "definition": "**Difficulty:** 1-3 · **Prerequisites:** Component Libraries: Material UI, Chip, Material UI component catalog, MUI Timeline component, Popper  This chapter opens with the Grid v2 migration, which renames the legacy grid (`@mui/material/Grid` in v6, `@mui/material/GridLegacy` in v7) and lands the new layout grid at `@mui/material/Grid` (v7) or `@mui/material/Grid2` (v6), with collapsed `size={{ xs, sm, md, ... }}` props and a removed `item` prop. Around the migration sits the rest of the MUI vocabulary the new grid composes with: `theme.typography` and the `Typography` and `Link` components that style every text node, the `Typography` `variantMapping` that decouples visual variant from semantic HTML, `responsiveFontSizes()` for media-query-driven type scales, the `theme.transitions.create()` and `getAutoHeightDuration()` helpers plus `theme.motion.reducedMotion` that keep motion consistent across the UI, `ImageList` (and its quilted / woven / masonry variants) for repeated image grids, `Tooltip` for accessible labels on hover / focus / long-press, and the `unstable_ClassNameGenerator` build-time hook that rewrites every MUI component class prefix across the app before any `@mui/*` import is evaluated.",
          "mental_model": "The new layout grid (Grid v2, also called the modern Grid) is the same flexbox idea as before: a `container` with `size`-driven children that break onto multiple lines at the theme breakpoints. What changed is the API surface. Per-breakpoint props collapsed into a single `size` object, the `item` flag disappeared, the `offset` feature replaced `zeroMinWidth`, and the grid now uses CSS variables instead of nested negative margins (so it no longer overflows the container). The migration is a one-time rewrite of an import path and a few prop names, with a codemod that does most of the rename for you.  subgraph v6 [MUI v6]     V6Import[\"import Grid from '@mui/material/Grid2'\"]     V6Props[\"size={{ xs: 12, sm: 6 }}\"]     V6Import --> V6Grid[\"Modern Grid (Grid2 import)\"]     V6Props --> V6Grid   end",
          "code_example": "bun add @mui/material @emotion/react @emotion/styled\nbun add @mui/icons-material",
          "pitfalls": "The codemod is keyed on the import path. Run it after the rename or it skips the file.  Either un-wrap the inner `<Grid>` (rename one of them), or do the prop rename by hand. The codemod's source-matcher only catches direct `<Grid>` JSX.  Missing weights fall back to browser synthetic bold / light, which never matches real Roboto. The MUI docs flag the four weights explicitly.  `hyphens-auto` is language-aware and depends on a `lang` attribute somewhere up the tree (the standard place is on `<html>` or the section root). A `<Typography lang=\"en\">` works for that node, but if you put `lang` only on the `Typography` and not on the surrounding `ImageList` or `Box`, the rest of the tree still uses the document language.  The Tailwind-style \"inverse variant\" trap carries over to the MUI transition components. `disablePrefersReducedMotion` is on every transition component; you set it on the single component you want, and `theme.motion.reducedMotion` handles the rest. Building a custom CSS rule that starts unconditional then patches the inverse is fragile; build the rule with `motion.reducedMotion === 'system'` and the `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` wrapper from the start."
        },
