        "total_duration_seconds": 646,
        "summary_notes": {
          "definition": "A courier form has three boxes you fill in: what is in the parcel, what the receipt will look like, and what you handed over at the counter. Get any of the three wrong and the paperwork still ships, but the person opening the parcel at the other end finds something they did not expect.  Every axios request method has the same three boxes, and they are type parameters:",
          "mental_model": "The typed-wrapper pattern from this chapter is the layer everything above it plugs into. TanStack Query's `queryFn` is typed by what your function returns, so `useQuery({ queryFn: () => getUser(id) })` infers `User` with no extra annotation; get the wrapper's return type wrong and every component reading that query is wrong too. React Hook Form's submit handler feeds your `CreateUserBody` type straight into `createUser`, and a mismatch between the form's field names and the body type surfaces at compile time instead of as a 422 in staging.  The class of bug this prevents is the silent envelope leak: an `AxiosResponse<User>` passed around as if it were a `User`, discovered three components later when someone reads `user.name` and gets `undefined`. The `isAxiosError` guard prevents the other common one, a `catch` block that assumes `error.response.status` exists and throws `TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'status')` the first time the network actually drops.",
          "code_example": "import axios, { type AxiosInstance } from \"axios\";\n\ninterface User {\n  id: number;\n  name: string;\n  email: string;\n}\n\nconst api: AxiosInstance = axios.create({\n  baseURL: \"https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com\",\n});\n\nconst response = await api.get<User>(\"/users/1\");\n\nresponse.data.name; // string\nresponse.status; // number\nresponse.headers[\"content-type\"]; // AxiosHeaderValue",
          "pitfalls": "**Typing the variable instead of the generic.** These are not the same:  The promise resolves to the envelope. Destructure `{ data }` or read `response.data`.  **Using `any` to silence the interceptor config error.** `api.interceptors.request.use((config: any) => ...)` compiles and throws away every guarantee on the config, including that `config.headers` has a `set` method. Name `InternalAxiosRequestConfig` instead.  **Assuming `T` validates the payload.** `api.get<User[]>(\"/users\")` on an endpoint that returns `{ items: User[] }` type-checks perfectly and then `users.map` throws:  The generic is your assertion, checked nowhere. Parse with a schema when the source is not under your control."
        },
