              "mental_model": "The advanced API surface is where TanStack Query differentiates from a hand-rolled `useEffect` + `fetch`. Five patterns show up in real codebases:  - **Global status indicators.** A `<NetworkIndicator>` driven by `useIsFetching`, paired with a `<MutationIndicator>` driven by `useIsMutationStatus`. The pattern is one component per global concern. - **Dashboards with N parallel entries.** `useQueries` (with `combine`) is the canonical shape for a dashboard. Each tile gets a row in the result array, and the consumer flattens or aggregates as needed. - **Infinite feeds.** `useInfiniteQuery` is the right hook for chat histories, search results, comment threads. The \"Load more\" pattern is one `fetchNextPage` button per page boundary. - **Dependent data.** A user → team, an order → customer, a project → members tree. `enabled` (or `skipToken`) expresses the waterfall explicitly and keeps TypeScript narrowing clean. - **SSR data transfer.** `dehydrate` on the server, `<HydrationBoundary>` on the client. The pattern removes the \"Loading…\" flash for every page that ships prefetched data.",
              "code_example": "import { useIsFetching } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\nimport type { ReactElement } from \"react\";\n\nexport function NetworkIndicator(): ReactElement {\n  const isFetching = useIsFetching();\n  return (\n    <div aria-live=\"polite\" aria-busy={isFetching > 0}>\n      {isFetching > 0 ? `Loading ${isFetching}…` : \"Idle\"}\n    </div>\n  );\n}",
