              "mental_model": "The advanced surface is where TanStack Query differentiates from a hand-rolled `useEffect` + `fetch`. Five patterns show up in real codebases:  - **Conditional fetches.** `skipToken` is the canonical \"do not fire until a value is ready\" pattern. Search boxes, dependent queries, lazy detail panels all use it. - **SSR handoff.** A server that prefetches and a client that hydrates from `dehydrate` give the user the first paint with no spinner. The consumer code is identical to CSR; the boundary is the only difference. - **Offline-first PWAs.** `persistQueryClient` with a sync or async persister keeps the cache alive across reloads. `IsRestoringProvider` makes the restore race-free. - **Streaming jobs.** `streamedQuery` is the canonical \"tokens arrive over time\" pattern. The reducer form folds chunks into a single derived value as they arrive. - **Suspense integration.** `useSuspenseQuery` removes the `isPending` branch from the consumer and routes errors to error boundaries. The trade-off is real boundaries and no `enabled`.",
              "code_example": "import { skipToken, useQuery } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\nimport type { ReactElement } from \"react\";\n\ninterface User { readonly id: number; readonly name: string; }\n\nasync function fetchUser(id: number, signal: AbortSignal): Promise<User> {\n  const res = await fetch(`/api/users/${id}`, { signal });\n  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`);\n  return (await res.json()) as User;\n}\n\nexport function UserPanel({ userId }: { userId: number | null }): ReactElement {\n  const { data, isPending } = useQuery({\n    queryKey: [\"user\", userId] as const,\n    queryFn: userId === null\n      ? skipToken\n      : ({ signal }) => fetchUser(userId, signal),\n  });\n\n  if (userId === null) return <p>Pick a user</p>;\n  if (isPending) return <p>Loading…</p>;\n  return <p>{data!.name}</p>;\n}",
