        "title": "TanStack Query SSR dehydration and hydration",
        "local_chapter_file": "021-tanstack-query-ssr-dehydration-and-hydration.md",
        "key_concepts": [
          "JavaScript primer: `Promise.all` for parallel prefetching",
          "The concept: three query clients, one dehydrated payload",
          "Minimal example",
          "Predict-the-render",
          "Request waterfalls, and which ones hydration fixes",
          "Parallel suspense queries"
        ],
        "total_duration_seconds": 454,
        "summary_notes": {
          "definition": "Difficulty: 3 to 4 · Prerequisites: Server State with TanStack Query, `queryOptions`, Queries and query result states, Invalidating queries after mutations, createAsyncThunk for side effects  A moving company packs your kitchen into labeled boxes, drives them across town, and unpacks them in the new kitchen. Nothing is cooked twice. The plates that existed before the move exist after it.",
          "mental_model": "Hydration is the difference between a page that shows content on the first paint and one that shows three spinners. It shows up in every framework integration you will read: Next.js App Router templates ship `providers.tsx` plus `<HydrationBoundary>`, TanStack Start does the same through its router, and Remix templates dehydrate from the `loader`.  The bugs it prevents are concrete. A module-scope `QueryClient` on a server leaks one user's data into another user's page. A mismatched query key between prefetch and component quietly does nothing, so the page looks fine in development and double-fetches in production. Default `staleTime` doubles the request count on every server-rendered page. A `useSuspenseQuery` stack turns three parallel requests into three serial ones, which nobody notices on localhost and everybody notices on mobile.",
          "code_example": "// pages/posts.tsx\nimport {\n  HydrationBoundary,\n  QueryClient,\n  dehydrate,\n  queryOptions,\n  useQuery,\n} from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\nimport type { DehydratedState } from \"@tanstack/react-query\";\nimport type { ReactElement } from \"react\";\n\nexport interface Post {\n  readonly id: number;\n  readonly title: string;\n}\n\nasync function getPosts(): Promise<ReadonlyArray<Post>> {\n  const response = await fetch(\"https://example.test/api/posts\");\n  if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`Posts request failed: ${response.status}`);\n  return (await response.json()) as ReadonlyArray<Post>;\n}\n\nexport const postsQueryOptions = () =>\n  queryOptions({\n    queryKey: [\"posts\"] as const,\n    queryFn: getPosts,\n  });\n\nexport async function getServerSideProps(): Promise<{\n  props: { dehydratedState: DehydratedState };\n}> {\n  const queryClient = new QueryClient();\n  await queryClient.prefetchQuery(postsQueryOptions());\n  return { props: { dehydratedState: dehydrate(queryClient) } };\n}\n\nfunction Posts(): ReactElement {\n  // No loading state on first paint: the cache already holds this entry.\n  const { data, status } = useQuery(postsQueryOptions());\n\n  if (status === \"pending\") return <p>Loading posts…</p>;\n  if (status === \"error\") return <p role=\"alert\">Could not load posts.</p>;\n\n  return (\n    <ul>\n      {data.map((post) => (\n        <li key={post.id}>{post.title}</li>\n      ))}\n    </ul>\n  );\n}\n\nexport default function PostsRoute({\n  dehydratedState,\n}: {\n  dehydratedState: DehydratedState;\n}): ReactElement {\n  return (\n    <HydrationBoundary state={dehydratedState}>\n      <Posts />\n    </HydrationBoundary>\n  );\n}",
          "pitfalls": "Direct DOM mutation or impure side effects during the render phase cause hydration mismatches, duplicate executions in Strict Mode, and stale closures. Always declare full dependency arrays in useEffect and never read state during render from outside the component tree."
        },
